# 📘 Project 2.0 Backend - Architecture & Development Guide

This document is your complete, step-by-step technical guide to the Project 2.0 backend. It explains every layer, feature, database model, external service, and API endpoint implemented in the system.

---

## 🏛️ System Architecture Overview

The backend is built using **Clean Architecture** (4 decoupled layers) and **SOLID Principles**:

```
src/
├── domain/                  # 1. Core business entities & mathematical algorithms (Zero external dependencies)
│   ├── entities/            # Pure TypeScript data structures (User, Room, Lifestyle, etc.)
│   └── services/            # Pure domain algorithms (RoomMatchCalculatorService)
├── application/             # 2. Business use cases & abstract interfaces
│   ├── interfaces/          # Repository and service contracts (IRoomRepository, IJwtService)
│   ├── dto/                 # Data Transfer Objects defining request/response structures
│   └── use-case/            # Single-responsibility workflows (auth, user, room, admin, etc.)
├── infrastructure/          # 3. External tools, database, and third-party integrations
│   ├── database/            # MongoDB connection & Mongoose schemas
│   ├── repository/          # Concrete database repositories implementing domain interfaces
│   └── services/            # Cloudinary, Nodemailer, Bcrypt, JWT, and OTP generators
└── presentation/            # 4. HTTP delivery layer (Web / API)
    ├── controller/          # Request handlers reading req.body/params and sending JSON responses
    ├── router/              # Express route definitions
    ├── middleware/          # Authentication & Error Handling middlewares
    └── utils/validators/    # Zod schema validation contracts
```

---

## 🗄️ Database Models (`src/infrastructure/database/model`)

All 6 models are implemented using **Modern Mongoose (`InferSchemaType` + `HydratedDocument`)** as a single source of truth:

1. **`UserModel.ts`**:
   - Fields: `email`, `firstName`, `lastName`, `hashedPassword`, `isVerified`, `isBlocked`, `role` (`"host"` | `"seeker"` | `"admin"` | `"none"`), `isAdmin`, `isOnboarded`, `dob`, `gender`, `occupation`, `bio`, `idCardUrl`, `selfieUrl`, `identityVerified`, `identityStatus` (`"pending"` | `"verified"` | `"rejected"` | `"none"`), `rejectionReason`.
   - Feature: Enforces unique lowercase email indexing, timestamps.
2. **`RoomModel.ts`**:
   - Fields: `hostId`, `title`, `roomType`, `monthlyRent`, `location`, `capacity`, `availabilityNotes`, `amenities`, `images` (Cloudinary CDN URLs), `description`, `isActive`.
3. **`SeekerPreferenceModel.ts`**:
   - Fields: `userId`, `preferredLocation`, `maxBudget`, `roomTypePreference`, `requiredAmenities`, `isActive`.
4. **`LifestyleModel.ts`**:
   - Fields: `userId` (ref to User), `smoking`, `drinking`, `sleepSchedule`, `diet`, `cleanliness`, `visitorPolicy`, `roommateGenderPref`.
5. **`NotificationModel.ts`**:
   - Fields: `userId`, `title`, `message`, `type` (`"admin_verification"` | `"interest_request"` | `"system"`), `isRead`.
6. **`OtpModel.ts`**:
   - Fields: `email`, `otp`, `expiresAt`, `createdAt`.
   - Feature: MongoDB **TTL index** (`expires: 600`) that automatically deletes expired OTP documents from database memory after 10 minutes.

---

## 🚀 Complete Feature Breakdown

### 1. Authentication & Security Module (`src/application/use-case/auth/`)
- **Sign Up (`SignUpUserUseCase.ts`)**:
  - Checks if user exists. If unverified, resets old OTPs.
  - Hashes passwords using `bcrypt` (10 salt rounds).
  - Generates a 6-digit random OTP and stores it in MongoDB.
  - Dispatches verification email via `nodemailer` (SMTP).
- **OTP Verification (`VerifyOtpUseCase.ts`)**:
  - Validates code and verifies expiration.
  - Sets `isVerified = true` and deletes used OTP records.
  - Issues a 7-day stateless JWT access token.
- **Login (`LoginUserUseCase.ts`)**:
  - Validates user credentials, checks blocked status, compares bcrypt hash, and returns JWT token + user profile.
- **Forgot Password Flow (`ForgotPasswordUseCase.ts`, `VerifyResetOtpUseCase.ts`, `ResetPasswordUseCase.ts`)**:
  - Sends reset OTP, validates OTP code, and safely updates new hashed password.
- **Google OAuth (`GoogleAuthUseCase.ts`)**:
  - Authenticates users signing in with Google.

### 2. User Onboarding & Profile System (`src/application/use-case/user/`)
- **Profile Details (`UpdateProfileUseCase.ts`)**:
  - Updates personal info (gender, occupation, bio).
  - **Date of Birth Validation**: Strictly enforces that date of birth cannot be in the future.
- **Lifestyle Preferences (`CreateLifestyleUseCase.ts`, `GetLifestyleUseCase.ts`)**:
  - Saves living habits (smoking, drinking, diet, sleep schedule, cleanliness, visitors).
- **Identity Upload (`UploadIdentityUseCase.ts`)**:
  - Accepts base64 encoded Government ID Card and Selfie photo.
  - Uses `CloudinaryService` to upload photos to secure CDN storage (`kuday_id_cards`, `kuday_selfies`).
  - Sets `identityStatus = "pending"` for Admin review.
- **Dual-Role Switching (`UpdateRoleUseCase.ts`)**:
  - Allows users to toggle between **Host** and **Seeker** roles.
  - **Post Invalidation**: When user switches role, their existing post in the opposite role is automatically disabled (`isActive = false`) to prevent confusion.

### 3. Property & Room Listings (`src/application/use-case/room/`)
- **Room Creation (`CreateRoomUseCase.ts`)**:
  - Host creates room listing with rent, capacity, location, notes, and amenities.
  - Automatically uploads multiple property photos to Cloudinary CDN (`kuday_rooms`).
- **Verified Room Discovery (`GetRoomsUseCase.ts`)**:
  - Queries active rooms from **Admin-Verified hosts**.
  - Fetches current seeker's preferences and lifestyle habits.
  - Runs the **Compatibility Calculation Engine** for each room.
  - Returns sorted rooms from highest match percentage to lowest.

### 4. Roommate Seeker Preferences (`src/application/use-case/seeker/`)
- **Preference Creation (`CreateSeekerPreferenceUseCase.ts`)**:
  - Seeker specifies location, maximum budget, room type, and required amenities.
- **Seeker Discovery for Hosts (`GetSeekerPreferencesUseCase.ts`)**:
  - Hosts can browse verified room seekers.
  - Evaluates match scores between host's room listing and seeker profiles.

### 5. Domain Compatibility Match Engine (`src/domain/services/RoomMatchCalculatorService.ts`)
A dedicated mathematical scoring algorithm calculating a 0% to 100% compatibility score:
- **Location Match (25% weight)**: Substring matching between room location and seeker preferred location.
- **Budget Match (25% weight)**: Full points if rent $\le$ seeker budget; partial points if within 10% budget flexibility.
- **Room Type Match (15% weight)**: Exact type match or preference set to `"any"`.
- **Amenities Match (15% weight)**: Overlap ratio between seeker's required amenities and room's provided amenities.
- **Lifestyle Match (20% weight)**: Compatibility checks on smoking, drinking, cleanliness, and sleep schedule.

### 6. Admin Portal & Verification Queue (`src/application/use-case/admin/`)
- **Admin Authentication (`AdminLoginUseCase.ts`)**:
  - Secure admin portal login.
- **Identity Review Queue (`VerifyUserIdentityUseCase.ts`)**:
  - Admin inspects submitted ID Card photos and selfie photos.
  - Admin can **Approve** (sets `identityVerified = true`, `identityStatus = "verified"`) or **Reject** with a custom reason.
  - Automatically dispatches in-app notification to the user informing them of admin's decision.
- **User Management & Metrics (`GetAllUsersUseCase.ts`, `ToggleBlockUserUseCase.ts`, `GetAdminStatsUseCase.ts`)**:
  - Block/unblock users, monitor system metrics (total users, verified hosts, active rooms).

### 7. In-App Notification System (`src/application/use-case/notification/`)
- **`CreateNotificationUseCase.ts`**:
  - Dispatches notifications for Interest Requests (when a user clicks "Send Interest") and Admin Verification updates.
- **`GetNotificationsUseCase.ts` & `MarkNotificationReadUseCase.ts`**:
  - Fetches unread notifications and marks alerts as read.

---

## 🔌 External Infrastructure Services (`src/infrastructure/services/`)

| Service File | Technology | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `CloudinaryService.ts` | Cloudinary SDK v2 | Uploads base64 encoded images to cloud CDN and returns HTTPS URLs. Avoids storing multi-megabyte images inside MongoDB documents. |
| `JwtServices.ts` | `jsonwebtoken` | Issues and verifies signed 7-day HMAC SHA-256 JWT access tokens for stateless authorization. |
| `HashingService.ts` | `bcrypt` | Hashes passwords with 10 salt rounds and securely verifies password attempts. |
| `NodemailerService.ts` | `nodemailer` (Gmail SMTP) | Connects to SMTP email service to send 6-digit OTP verification codes to real user inboxes. |
| `OtpServices.ts` | Node.js `crypto` | Generates cryptographically secure 6-digit numeric OTP codes. |

---

## 📡 API Endpoints Reference

### 1. Authentication (`/api/auth`)
- `POST /api/auth/signUp` — Register a new account and dispatch OTP email.
- `POST /api/auth/verify-otp` — Verify 6-digit OTP and issue JWT access token.
- `POST /api/auth/login` — Login with email and password.
- `POST /api/auth/forgot-password` — Send password reset OTP.
- `POST /api/auth/verify-reset-otp` — Verify password reset OTP.
- `POST /api/auth/reset-password` — Set new password.
- `POST /api/auth/google` — Sign in / sign up with Google OAuth.

### 2. User & Onboarding (`/api/users`)
- `GET /api/users/profile/:userId` — Fetch user profile and verification status.
- `PUT /api/users/profile` — Update personal details (DOB, gender, occupation, bio).
- `PUT /api/users/role` — Switch role between Host and Seeker (auto-disables previous post).
- `POST /api/users/upload-identity` — Upload ID Card & Selfie for admin verification.

### 3. Lifestyle (`/api/lifestyle`)
- `POST /api/lifestyle` — Create or update lifestyle habits.
- `GET /api/lifestyle/:userId` — Fetch lifestyle habits for a user.

### 4. Room Listings (`/api/rooms`)
- `POST /api/rooms` — Create or update a host room listing with Cloudinary images.
- `GET /api/rooms?userId=:userId` — Fetch verified room listings with dynamic match scores.
- `GET /api/rooms/host/:hostId` — Fetch rooms created by a specific host.

### 5. Seeker Preferences (`/api/seeker-preferences`)
- `POST /api/seeker-preferences` — Save seeker home search preferences.
- `GET /api/seeker-preferences?userId=:userId` — Fetch verified room seekers with compatibility scores.
- `GET /api/seeker-preferences/user/:userId` — Fetch preferences for a specific seeker.

### 6. Notifications (`/api/notifications`)
- `POST /api/notifications` — Create an interest request or system alert.
- `GET /api/notifications/:userId` — Fetch all notifications for a user.
- `PATCH /api/notifications/:id/read` — Mark single notification as read.
- `PATCH /api/notifications/user/:userId/read-all` — Mark all notifications as read.

### 7. Admin (`/api/admin`)
- `POST /api/admin/login` — Admin login.
- `GET /api/admin/stats` — Fetch dashboard system stats.
- `GET /api/admin/users` — Fetch all registered users with filter/search.
- `PATCH /api/admin/users/:userId/block` — Toggle block/unblock status.
- `PATCH /api/admin/users/:userId/verify-identity` — Approve or reject user ID documents.

---

## 🧪 Testing & Code Verification

To verify that the entire backend compiles without TypeScript errors:
```bash
cd backend
npx tsc --noEmit
```

To run the development server:
```bash
npm run dev
```